  exp: "The patient is experiencing Pulseless Electrical Activity (PEA), defined as the presence of organized electrical activity on the monitor without a palpable pulse. PEA is a 'non-shockable' cardiac arrest rhythm. The ACLS protocol for PEA and Asystole requires continuous high-quality CPR, securing the airway, searching for reversible causes (the 'Hs and Ts'), and administering Intravenous Epinephrine 1 mg every 3 to 5 minutes immediately.",
  wrongExp: "• <strong>Option A (Defibrillation):</strong> Defibrillation is completely contraindicated in PEA and Asystole; it is only for VF and pulseless VT.<br>• <strong>Option B (Synchronized cardioversion):</strong> Cardioversion is used for patients with a PULSE who have unstable tachyarrhythmias (e.g., unstable SVT, AFib, or VT with a pulse).<br>• <strong>Option C (Intravenous Atropine):</strong> Atropine was removed from the ACLS cardiac arrest algorithm for PEA/Asystole in 2010. It is now only used for symptomatic bradycardia with a pulse."
