  chapter: "Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation (CPR)",
  level: "Easy",
  q: "A 55-year-old male in the ICU develops a rapid palpitation. The ECG monitor shows a monomorphic ventricular tachycardia at 180 bpm. His blood pressure is 70/40 mmHg, and he is diaphoretic and confused. A peripheral pulse is palpable but weak. What is the most appropriate electrical therapy?",
  opts: ["Unsynchronized defibrillation at 200 Joules", "Synchronized cardioversion", "Transcutaneous pacing", "Administration of a precordial thump"],
