  exp: "Neuromuscular blocking agents (NMBAs), such as rocuronium and succinylcholine, are the most common cause of true IgE-mediated anaphylactic reactions in the perioperative period (accounting for roughly 50-60% of cases). This is believed to be due to cross-sensitization to the quaternary ammonium epitope present in NMBAs, which is also found in many everyday cosmetics, soaps, and foods. Antibiotics are the second most common cause.",
