  opts: ["PaCO2 rises above 45 mmHg or increases by 10 mmHg from baseline", "PaCO2 rises above 60 mmHg or increases by 20 mmHg over baseline", "PaO2 falls below 60 mmHg or O2 saturation drops below 85%", "Arterial pH drops below 7.20 regardless of PaCO2"],
  ans: 1,
  exp: "The apnea test is the ultimate clinical test for brainstem function in brain death determination. It assesses whether the respiratory center in the medulla responds to the maximal physiological stimulus: hypercapnia. A positive apnea test (confirming absent respiratory drive/brain death) is defined as the absolute lack of respiratory effort despite the PaCO2 reaching ≥ 60 mmHg or increasing by ≥ 20 mmHg over the pre-test baseline.",
  wrongExp: "• <strong>Option A (PaCO2 > 45 or +10):</strong> This threshold is too low and does not represent a maximal stimulus to the medullary respiratory center.<br>• <strong>Option C (PaO2 falls below 60):</strong> Hypoxia is not the primary driver tested in the apnea test, and severe hypoxia invalidates the test (it must be aborted if the patient becomes hemodynamically unstable or severely hypoxic).<br>• <strong>Option D (pH drops below 7.20):</strong> Acidosis will occur secondary to hypercapnia, but the strict diagnostic criterion relies specifically on the PaCO2 value."
